que polling data, analyses of how the press used the hacked content, and a synthesis of half a century of media effects research to argue that, although not certain, it is probable that the Russians helped elect the 45th president of the United States.In the process, Cyberwar tackles questions that include: How extensive was the troll messaging? What characteristics of the social media platforms did the Russians exploit? Why did the mainstream press rush the hacked content into the citizenry's newsfeeds? Was Clinton telling the truth when she alleged that the debate moderators distorted what she said in the leaked speeches? Did the Russian influence extend beyond social media and news to alter the behavior of FBI director James Comey?\"--Dust jacket flap.","primaryTopic":"Democracy & Elections","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Politics & Government","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Politics & Government","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Politics & Government","mappedSubject":"Politics & Government","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores the impact of Russian interference in the 2016 presidential election through political and media lenses, making Politics & Government the dominant subject with American History and Journalism & Reportage as relevant secondary subjects.","id":"subject-evidence-book-cyberwar-how-russian-hackers-and-trolls-helped-elect-a-president-kathleen-hall-jamieson-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Trump, donald, 1946-","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-cyberwar-how-russian-hackers-and-trolls-helped-elect-a-president-kathleen-hall-jamieson","id":"subject-evidence-book-cyberwar-how-russian-hackers-and-trolls-helped-elect-a-president-kathleen-hall-jamieson-5"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Mas